            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Urdu for a printer, then the Urdu for a charger."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ساڑی",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ساڑی — sāṛī — \"a sari\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ساڑی (sāṛī) is a tadbhava, a word inherited from Sanskrit and reshaped by sound change. It comes from śāṭī, \"strip of cloth, garment\" (CDIAL 12381). CDIAL notes that the word also travelled west, to Pashto and to Persian shāl, the source of English shawl."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
